1018..1096 Comment "/// Rotating by `b` and back is the identity (cubical\'s `rotInv-1`, `b · a ·"
1097..1177 Comment "/// invLooper b ≡ a`, `_·_` associating to the left). The obligation over `a`"
1178..1252 Comment "/// holds `b` at its point, where `mul(Base, a)` is `a` and the loop moves"
1253..1325 Comment "/// through `mul`\'s second argument as itself; the one over `b` moves it"
1326..1401 Comment "/// through both of the outer `mul`\'s arguments, the loop then its inverse."
1402..1478 Comment "/// The square of the two loops is not owed: the paths of the circle are its"
1479..1496 Comment "/// words, a set."
